  "finalText": "Frames look clean now. I'm doing a last check on the end card, then I'll wrap up.\nThe **Pulse 2** title sequence is built: 10 s at 30 fps, cut to 120 BPM (0.5 s per beat). I checked it frame by frame in contact sheets. The layout checker only flags the \"PULSE 2\" layer box, which is wider than the visible text, and off-canvas wipe bars between sweeps, which is expected.\n\n- **Feature flashes (0.5 s, 1.5 s, 2.5 s):** \"40h battery\", \"Spatial audio\" and \"Pure silence\" each land on a beat. Each punches in from 150% scale and snaps out on the next beat. A full-frame orange wipe bar sweeps through at every cut, and a small orange beat dot pulses along the bottom.\n- **Slam (4.0 s):** on the bar downbeat the frame flashes orange. **PULSE 2** drops in from 320% scale, with a short shake. An orange shockwave ring and a thinner white ring expand and fade behind it.\n- **CTA (6.5 s onward):** the orange pill springs in, \"Available now\" rises into it in dark text, and the pill gives a gentle breathing pulse until the end.\n\nThe look is #0A0A0C background, #FF5A1F orange and #F5F5F7 text, in Inter 900, with fast ease-out entrances and ease-in exits.\n\nI fixed two problems after the first check: the name and words were fading in early, and the rings were filling blue.\n\nThe animation ends at 9 s, so the last second is a held end card. I can add a beat-synced exit or tighten the timing if you want."
